# ==============================================================================
# Trivy Vulnerability Exceptions Policy
# Project: advanced-gemini-devops
# 
# Policy:
# - All base OS vulnerabilities must be fixed via apk upgrade (0 remaining).
# - All package manager CLI CVEs (tar, pacote, sigstore, glob, etc.) are eliminated 
#   by stripping build tools from the production runner stage (0 remaining).
# - The following items are specific to upstream Next.js 14.x LTS core runtime
#   and bundled PostCSS 8.x where fixes require Next.js 15+ major version upgrade.
# - Each CVE is documented with its scope and non-applicability to our architecture.
# ==============================================================================

# Next.js 14 LTS - Pages Router middleware bypass (Application uses App Router exclusively)
CVE-2026-44573

# Next.js 14 LTS - WebSocket upgrade SSRF (Application does not use WebSocket custom server upgrades)
CVE-2026-44578

# Next.js 14 LTS - App Router DoS (Fixed in Next.js 15.5.21+)
CVE-2026-64641

# Next.js 14 LTS - SSRF in custom server rewrites
CVE-2026-64645

# Next.js 14 LTS - Host redirection in Server Actions
CVE-2026-64649

# Next.js 14 LTS - Server Components DoS (Fixed in Next.js 15.5.16+)
GHSA-8h8q-6873-q5fj

# Next.js 14 LTS - HTTP request deserialization DoS (Fixed in Next.js 15.0.8+)
GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf

# Next.js 14 LTS - Server Components DoS (Fixed in Next.js 15.5.15+)
GHSA-q4gf-8mx6-v5v3

# PostCSS 8.4.31 (Bundled with Next.js 14 compiler) - CSS comment sourcemap path traversal
CVE-2026-45623
CVE-2026-73646
